body:
The README says "Tested on Linux; macOS and Windows builds are not yet tested much". If you have a Mac (Apple Silicon or Intel), install the `.dmg` from the latest release (right-click → Open, it is unsigned) and report here:

- the first run (organization, template, a model key), Home and creating a task;
- an agency with Claude Code, Codex or Gemini CLI workers running one card (sign-in or key);
- the Files editor (tabs, save, git), Preview (a page, an image, a PDF) and dark mode;
- the window title bar: traffic lights at the right place, both drag strips drag;
- anything that looks wrong at 1024 px wide.

Screenshots welcome. Each problem you find becomes its own issue; link them here.

The README says "Tested on Linux; macOS and Windows builds are not yet tested much". If you run Windows 10 or 11, install the `-windows-x64-setup.exe` from the latest release (More info → Run anyway, it is unsigned) and report here:

- the first run (organization, template, a model key), Home and creating a task;
- an agency with Claude Code, Codex or Gemini CLI workers running one card (the adapters are installed with npm; the `.cmd` shims must be found);
- the Files editor (tabs, save, git with Git for Windows), Preview and dark mode;
- the window buttons (minimise, maximise, close) and the two drag strips;
- the in-app updater, if a newer release exists while you test.

Screenshots welcome. Each problem you find becomes its own issue; link them here.
